From dc4400e2a4120545c3bca41164722f8610316b1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (audit)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:20:11 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] mobile: homework review/split via the API, https-only
 release, safer exam drafts

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011d4mgSxngjRmAXosGe4ry4

- Tutors could not see what a student handed in: the card now opens the
  submitted link or file (new submission_file_url from the API).
- 'Split per student' calls POST /homework/<id>/split/ (atomic) instead of
  N creates + delete; the success toast was never shown (computed before the
  loop ran).
- Students cannot resubmit checked homework (matches the server rule); clearer
  'Submit homework' / 'Update submission' labels.
- Release builds no longer allow cleartext http (debug/profile still do, for a
  server on the local network); release default server is the hosted https
  API, overridable with --dart-define=API_BASE_URL.
- A typed server address without a scheme gets https unless it is local.
- Exam drafts are keyed per account (shared phones leaked answers between
  students); an unexpected error no longer leaves 'Turn in' stuck.
- setState/context after awaits guarded where they were not.
- New offline tests: test/contract_test.dart.
